    "narrative": {
      "care_continuity": [
        "SitRep82 publishes no patient-movement table; the national isolation census of 674 comes from the cover, with only Ituri (468) and Nord-Kivu (186) splitting confirmed from suspected.",
        "Haut-Uele reports no isolation census at all this cycle, so it is absent from the 674 rather than counted as zero; Tshopo's 3 and Sud-Kivu's 17 are unclassified.",
        "Only Ituri publishes a bed denominator: 468 patients on 833 beds, 56.2% occupancy, with three CTE over confirmed-case saturation (Nizi 233%, ISTM 147%, Bambu 140%) and Logo at 150% for suspects.",
        "The 120-bed Rwankole CTE was officially launched, but a provider strike at CTE CME and hygienist unrest at Rwampara disrupted admissions the same day.",
        "Nord-Kivu reports cumulative intra-CTE mortality of 36% across 187 admissions, and none of its 12 confirmed-case households were decontaminated."
      ],
      "highlights": [
        "The footprint holds at 51 of 140 health zones; no new zone was affected in the last 24 hours.",
        "The DRC headline is 3973 confirmed / 1801 deaths; all 51 printed rows close exactly to those totals and every province total matches Tableau 1.",
        "Confirmed movement is clean at +99, but the death cumulative advances only 50 against 52 notified: SitRep 81's Nord-Kivu provincial total carried a two-death excess over its own zone rows, resorbed here. Row-to-row the movement is exactly +52.",
        "Ituri supplies 85 of the 99 new confirmations and 47 of the 52 deaths; Nord-Kivu now contributes only 10.1% of new cases but holds a 67.0% fatality ratio against Ituri's 42.3%.",
        "37 of the 52 deaths (71.2%) occurred in the community, up from 63.6% the previous day.",
        "Contact follow-up falls to 75.3% and alert investigation to 65.6%; Ituri investigated only 279 of its 569 alerts (49.0%).",
        "Nord-Kivu records its highest weekly notification count of the outbreak in week 31 (101 cases, after 82 in week 30)."
      ]
    },
